Set correct origin for internal redirects in custom server (CVE-2026-64649)

Backport of upstream vercel/next.js commit b51206321854193208c0805ba42acc49287f942b
([16.x] Set correct origin for internal redirects in custom server) to next 16.2.9.

Fixes an SSRF (CWE-918) in Server Actions on custom servers: the outbound
request origin for forwarded/redirected actions was derived from
Host-associated request headers, allowing an attacker who controls the Host
header to steer server-issued requests to an arbitrary host. The origin is now
resolved from the trusted initURL request metadata instead of the request host.

Dist-based patching: next is installed from npm, which ships only the
compiled output under dist/ (no packages/next/src or errors.json), so the fix
is applied directly to dist/server/app-render/action-handler.js and its ESM
counterpart dist/esm/server/app-render/action-handler.js.

